    {
      "id": "133bd901-e3dc-4d08-be8e-56155c029f58",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Reflection\n\nThis project helped me understand how functions make programs more organized and reusable. Instead of placing all conditions directly in the main program, I learned how functions can simplify and structure code better.\n\nI also liked this project because it felt personal to me. I’ve always been drawn to chemistry because of how systematic and interconnected everything feels, especially in the periodic table. Even though every element has different properties and behaviors, they still belong to a larger structure.\n\nIn a way, I think that idea resonates with how I view people and systems too — different identities, different behaviors, but still connected under something bigger.\n\nMaking this project made programming feel less mechanical and more meaningful because I was able to connect it to something I genuinely find interesting.",
      "metadata": {}
